+# The ambient light sensor's colour temperature moves the display's white point as macOS's True Tone
+# does: STRENGTH of the way from the panel's white toward the room's colour, as a full 3x3 colour
+# matrix sent to the panel's own white-point adaptation (the display driver's panel_adaptation).
+# The driver multiplies it with the compositor's colour matrix, so Omarchy's night light keeps its
+# own matrix and the two add up (adaptation x night light), as macOS adds up True Tone and Night
+# Shift. Each change runs macOS's ramp: one matrix per frame along its eased 1.9 s curve.
+# Runs as a system service only on a Mac with a table in /usr/share/omarchy-mac/truetone (named after
